course: dictionary
lesson: 9749
title: Superlatives: the top one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A superlative is the form of an adjective that names the top one of three or more things. «Mia is the tallest girl in the class.» Tallest is the superlative of tall: it means taller than all the others.
explain: Short adjectives add -est: fast, fastest; big, biggest (double the g). Long adjectives use most: beautiful, most beautiful. Compare with the comparative, which only compares two: «Mia is taller than Sam» uses taller.
explain: Some words change completely and must be learned by heart: good, better, best; bad, worse, worst.
explain: Adverbs can be superlative too: «Ravi ran the fastest of all.» If you can say "the ___ of all", you probably need a superlative.
fact: A superlative names the most or least of three or more things.
fact: Short adjectives take -est: «the biggest», «the fastest».
fact: Long adjectives use most: «the most beautiful», «the most helpful».
fact: Irregular superlatives: good, better, best; bad, worse, worst.
fact: A superlative can also mean of the highest quality: «a superlative performance»; reviews can be full of superlatives, which is very high praise.
exercise: What is the superlative of tall? | taller | *tallest | tallish | most tall
exercise: Which sentence uses the superlative form? | *Sam is the fastest runner in the team. | Sam and Ben run fast together. | Sam is faster than Ben. | Sam runs fast.
exercise: What is the superlative of good? | gooder | more good | *best | goodest
test: Complete the sentence: «This is the ___ mountain in the country.» (high) | *highest | higher | most high
test: Complete the sentence: «Ella was the ___ at spelling in the whole school.» (good) | gooder | more good | *best
exam: Complete the sentence: «Our dog is the ___ dog in the street.» (bad) | most bad | *worst | worser | badest
